      "id": "m04",
      "question": "How do I access the web sources a model used for its answer?",
      "inScope": true,
      "askedAt": "2026-09-29T18:00:46.529Z",
      "classification": "answered-with-citations",
      "answer": "For `generateText`, access the sources through `result.sources`. Each URL source includes an `id`, `url`, optional `title`, and `providerMetadata`. [1: \"When you use `generateText`, you can access the sources using the `sources` property\"]\n\nFor `streamText`, inspect `result.stream` for parts where `part.type === 'source'` and `part.sourceType === 'url'`; source details include the ID, title, URL, and provider metadata. [1: \"if (part.type === 'source' && part.sourceType === 'url')\"]\n\nSources are currently limited to web pages that ground the response, and they’re also available through the `result.sources` promise. [1: \"Currently sources are limited to web pages that ground the response\"]",
