    {
      "id": "m08",
      "question": "How do I ask the user to approve a tool call before it runs?",
      "inScope": true,
      "askedAt": "2026-09-29T18:01:05.750Z",
      "classification": "answered-with-citations",
      "answer": "Configure `toolApproval` on `generateText`, `streamText`, or `ToolLoopAgent` to return `'user-approval'` for the tool call. [2: \"Configure approval with `toolApproval` on `generateText`, `streamText`, or `ToolLoopAgent`.\"] For a per-tool rule, set that tool’s status to `'user-approval'`; you can also use an async callback to decide based on the input. [2: \"You can make approval decisions based on tool input by providing an async function\"]\n\nThe first call completes with a `tool-approval-request` in the result; it does not pause while waiting. Show the request to the user, collect their decision, then add a `tool-approval-response` to the messages and call the model again. If approved, the tool runs; if denied, the model receives the denial. [2: \"the manual approval flow requires two calls to the model\"]",
      "citations": [
        {
          "type": "citation",
          "n": 2,
          "quote": "Configure approval with `toolApproval` on `generateText`, `streamText`, or `ToolLoopAgent`.",
