    {
      "id": "m11",
      "question": "How do I define a tool whose schema is only known at runtime?",
      "inScope": true,
      "askedAt": "2026-09-29T18:01:12.855Z",
      "classification": "answered-with-citations",
      "answer": "Use `dynamicTool` for tools whose schemas are not known at compile time. [1: \"AI SDK Core supports dynamic tools for scenarios where tool schemas are not known at compile time.\"] Provide an `inputSchema` and an `execute` function; the input is typed as `unknown`, so validate or cast it at runtime before using it. [1: \"input is typed as 'unknown'\"] For example, create the tool with `dynamicTool({ description, inputSchema, execute })`. [1: \"The `dynamicTool` helper creates tools with unknown input/output types:\"]",
