      "id": "m12",
      "question": "What timeout should I set for video generation?",
      "inScope": true,
      "askedAt": "2026-09-29T18:01:21.490Z",
      "classification": "answered-with-citations",
      "answer": "Video generation typically takes longer than image generation, so consider a timeout of 60 seconds or more, depending on the model and video length. [1: \"Consider using longer timeouts (60 seconds or more) depending on the model and video length.\"] You can set it with `AbortSignal.timeout(...)` via `abortSignal`. [1: \"that you can use to abort the video generation process or set a timeout.\"] If you mean the polling timeout, its documented default is 600,000 ms (10 minutes), configurable with `poll.timeoutMs`. [2: \"timeoutMs: 600000, // Timeout after 10 minutes (default)\"]",
