    {
      "id": "m15",
      "question": "How can a tool send a screenshot back to the model?",
      "inScope": true,
      "askedAt": "2026-09-29T18:01:28.255Z",
      "classification": "answered-with-citations",
      "answer": "Return the screenshot from the tool’s `execute` function as a file result, then use `toModelOutput` to convert it into a model-readable content part. [1: \"AI SDK Core tools have an optional `toModelOutput` function that converts the tool result into a content part.\"] For example, return the image’s base64 data with `type: 'file'` and an image media type, then map it to a file part whose data uses `{ type: 'data', data: ... }`. [1: \"data: { type: 'data', data: output.data }\"] For Google, the docs specify base64 inline-data file parts or base64 `data:` URLs; remote HTTP(S) URLs in tool-result URL parts are not supported. [1: \"Remote HTTP(S) URLs in tool-result URL parts are not supported.\"]",
      "citations": [
        {
          "type": "citation",
